B.MQ=new A.bS(B.NG,["Choice of map type","Please enlarge your screen to be able to use this version!","","TG","RNI","Protected harmonious landscape","New ADF Mamimahefa limits","Pasture","Nexus","BE","RVI","AF","RSP","SB","PAI","TGRN","Download the mobile version","You cannot select more than two municipalities.","You cannot select more than two districts.","See the details of the plot","You must select at least one municipality.","You must select at least one district.","Zoom in","Zoom out","Go left","Go right","Go to top","Go down","Select all","Deselect all","Reset filtering","French","English","Home","Filter","Selection by radius","Use map","Land-FLR catalogue","Help","Context","Overlapping plots.","Please disable the radius selection.","Downloading GeoJson","Authentication","E-mail address :","Password :","Attempting to connect","User not found.","Incorrect password.","You are offline.","Please fill out the field.","Authenticate","Land tenures","Land tenure","FLR options","FLR Option","Choice of data type","No Region","Choice of District","GeoJson data by municipality","Show land tenure informations","Show information by FLR option","Means of access to resources","Allocation to CTDs","Allocation","Immatriculation - Direct management","Immatriculation - Land acquisition","Temporary occupation","Concession","Delegation of management","Management transfer","Free provision of land for building rights","Ordinary lease","Emphyteutic lease","Lease of reforestation areas with associated forest resources (> 5 000 ha)","Emphyteutic lease for land reserves for reforestation or approved land for reforestation","Lease management of Koloala sites (area <1 000 ha)","Lease / Sub-lease","Land reforestation reserves","Acquisition of land reserves for reforestation or land approved for reforestation","Options for securing land rights","Registration","Collective registration","Individual registration - free transfer","Individual land certification","Collective land certification","Natural public land","Allocated land","Registered land in the name of the State",u.M,"Private property owned by CTDs or EPAs","Titled private property","Registered private property","Certified land",u.M,"Untitled private property","Land reserved for investment","Public protected areas","Mixed protected areas","Approved protected areas","Community management sites","Sustainable forest management sites (Koloala)","National forest estate outside protected areas (PA)","Land used for wood energy and timber production","Demand","Demand FN","FN","RMt","Certificate of recognition","Reforestation on degraded land","Restoration of degraded natural forests","Restoration of degraded mangroves","Restoration of agroforestry landscapes","Agriculture","Inhabited area","Grazing management","Restoration of degraded land","Restoration of water resources","Bamboo planting","Restoration of degraded rainforests","Restoration of degraded riparian forests","Restoration of degraded dry forests","Not applicable","List of regions","(Downloading data)","Loading data","List of districts","List of municipalities","Preparing the display of data","Completed","Municipality","Downloading the map","Data downloaded.","Selection of region","Success","Error","No plots found.","The radius should not exceed 5000.","Selection of districts","Next","Cancel","Selection of municipalities","Loading","Filter options","Filter","Tiles","Tile","Show all","Hide all","Legend of colors","(Depending on available land tenure status)","Radius","Work area","Reduce","Region :","Districts :","Municipalities :","Geographic coordinates:","Plot details","No land tenure","Vocation","Risk of conflict","Not mentioned","Not mentioned","Low","Medium","High","Number","No title","Date obtained","Capacity","Property name","Cf\xb0 number","Area in hectare","Plot details (PLOF)","Why an application on land and FLR options?","The data on the plots used in this application are based on the following data sources: DRDAT, D(i)REDD, land tenure offices, and updated Local Land Use Plans (PLOF). The spatial data used in this application are presented exactly as received from their respective sources, without any modification, alteration, or adaptation to their content. For example, there may be overlaps as well as accuracy errors. The application disclaims all responsibility for the accuracy, quality, or relevance of the information contained on the map.\n\nGiven the dynamic nature of land information, regular corrections or updates will be carried out by the authorities managing the application.","Land tenure issues are of critical importance in Madagascar, where deforestation is advancing rapidly. This situation is often linked to the search for new land by vulnerable populations, who adopt unsuitable production methods.\n\nIn this context, since 2017, German Development Cooperation has been supporting the Malagasy government in implementing the 'Promotion of Responsible Tenure Policy' project (ProPFR). This project aims to establish a link between land tenure security and the sustainable enhancement of forest landscape restoration to encourage the responsible use of natural and forest resources. Ensuring that rightful owners can enjoy their land is seen as a lever to promote sustainable investments, thereby contributing to the global fight against hunger.\n\nAs part of this project, a Land-FLR (Forest Landscape Restoration) Catalogue was developed, including a synthetic matrix. This reference document proposes pilot measures based on FLR options outlined in the national strategy and serves as a working tool for various FLR stakeholders. It provides an overview of opportunities for formalizing legitimate land rights, providing key information on current land classifications, types of access to land and forest resources, and options for securing acquired rights. Finally, this document also serves as a guide for implementing the FLR strategy at both regional and national levels.\n\nFollowing the validation of this catalogue and its matrix, requests from technical staff and FLR projects/programs led to the idea of making it interactive and accessible in the form of a digital application, a decision-support tool designed for practical use. This is how the application was born.","For more information or further assistance on securing tenure rights,please contact the ProPFR project directly.","Promoting of responsible land policy project (ProPFR)","A project supported by the German federal government through the Deutsche Gesellschaft f\xfcr Internationale Zusammenarbeit (GIZ) GmbH.","ProPFR national office Antananarivo","In collaboration with ECO Consult GmbH & Co. KG, GOPA, and Land Resources.","In partnership with:","Frequently asked questions (FAQ)","1. The area considered by the application","The operational part of the ProPFR project is being implemented in the Boeny and Diana regions, located in the northwest and north of Madagascar. The area considered by the application includes in the beginning spatial data from the municipalities and districts within these two regions. However, the application is designed so that spatial data from other regions can be added in the future.","2. The update and reliability of the spatial information","The spatial data reflect the land tenure situation of the areas considered at the time of the last update of the application. The spatial data comes from official Malagasy sources and is displayed without modification. Given the dynamic nature of tenure information, corrections or updates will be made by the authorities managing the application.\nData on the land plots used are based on the following sources: DRDAT, D(i)REDD, land offices, based on latest available local land use plans (PLOF). It is planned to update them at regular intervals for the application.","3. Who is the target user of this application?","At this stage, the identified target groups are: i) staff from decentralized technical services: DRDAT, DRAE, D(i)REDD (especially at the district level), ii) technicians from NGOs working in partnership with GIZ projects in the Boeny and DIANA regions or others, and iii) teams from German-Malagasy cooperation projects/programs (F4F, PADDI, ProSol).."],t.li)
